  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many apples Tom has, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify how many apples Ben has.\n2. Use the information about Ben's apples to find out how many apples Tom has.\n\nStep 1: Determine how many apples Ben has.\nWe know that Ben has 8 apples more than Phillip. Since Phillip has 40 apples, we can calculate the number of apples Ben has as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Ben's apples} = \\text{Phillip's apples} + 8 = 40 + 8 = 48 \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine how many apples Tom has.\nWe know that Tom has three eighths as many apples as Ben. Therefore, we can calculate the number of apples Tom has as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Tom's apples} = \\frac{3}{8} \\times \\text{Ben's apples} = \\frac{3}{8} \\times 48 = 18 \\]\n\nSo, Tom has \\(\\boxed{18}\\) apples.",
